# The build context must stay tiny: data/ alone is 24 GB (lake + journals) and is BIND-MOUNTED
# at runtime, never baked into the image. Secrets are injected at runtime too — never layered.
#
# Markdown is deliberately NOT excluded: pyproject sets `readme = "README.md"`, so hatchling
# needs it in the context to build the project (a `*.md` + `!README.md` pair did not survive
# buildkit's matcher, and the docs are a few hundred KB — not worth the fragility).
data/
.env
.env.*
.git/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
backups/
research/**/results_*.json
